{{also|Politesse}}

==English==
===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|politesse|lang=fr}}, from the {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|politezza|lang=it}}, from {{term|polito|lang=it}}, past participle of {{term|pulire||lang=it|to polish”, “to clean}}, from the {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|polire||lang=la}}, present active infinite form of {{term|polio|poliō|I polish”, “I smooth|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɒlɪˈtɛs/}}
*{{a|US}} {{IPA|/pɑləˈtɛs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[civility|Civility]], [[politeness]], [[courtesy]] or [[gallantry]]; or an instance of this.
#* '''1978''', Iris Murdoch, ''The Sea, The Sea'', Vintage 1999, pp. 56-7:
#*: The reference in his letter to ‘having a drink’ is of course just an empty '''''politesse'''''.

